codex
The 1974 Hehl paper gives a concrete averaging requirement: each macroscopically small fluid element must contain many particles. It also gives a length-scale condition for averaging away a spin–vorticity term, though that is not a general validity bound.

Published spin-hydrodynamics papers show that shear can generate momentum-dependent polarisation. They do not establish what happens in a strongly sheared Einstein–Cartan collapse at the fluid turning point; I’ll keep that distinction explicit.
